---
title: Bucket collection
layout: home
description: Things to do — grouped, checked off, and left on the page once they are done, because a list that deletes what you achieved is a to-do list and not a record of anything.
eyebrow: Collections · Bucket list
source: src/components/life.css
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap" style="padding-top: 1.5rem; --im-section-gap: 1.5rem">
	<p class="im-eyebrow">Collections · Bucket list · {{page.title}}</p>
	<p class="im-lede">{{page.description}}</p>
	<p class="doc-source"><code>{{page.source}}</code></p>
</section>

<div class="im-single im-wrap" data-sidebar="on">
	<article class="im-stack" style="--im-stack-gap: 2rem">
		<header class="im-collhead">
			<p class="im-eyebrow">Bucket list</p>
			<h1 class="im-collhead-title">Things I want to do</h1>
			<p class="im-collhead-text">Kept in public because a list nobody can see is a list you can quietly drop. One is done, two are booked, and the rest are honest about being someday.</p>
			<p class="im-collhead-meta"><span>{{demo.wishlist.length}} things</span><span>1 done</span><span>2 booked</span></p>
		</header>

		<div class="im-collbar">
			<div class="im-collbar-filters">
				<a class="im-tag" href="#bucket" aria-current="page">Everything</a>
				<a class="im-tag" href="#bucket">Water</a>
				<a class="im-tag" href="#bucket">Cold</a>
				<a class="im-tag" href="#bucket">Distance</a>
				<a class="im-tag" href="#bucket">Done</a>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="im-stack" id="bucket" style="--im-stack-gap: 2rem">
			<section class="im-bucket-group">
				<p class="im-bucket-head"><span>Water</span><span>1 of 3 done</span></p>
				<ul class="im-buckets">
					{{#each demo.wishlist}}{{#match group "=" "Water"}}
					<li class="im-bucket"{{#if state}} data-state="{{state}}"{{/if}}>
						<span class="im-bucket-mark">{{icon "check"}}</span>
						<p class="im-bucket-title"><a href="/collections/wishlist/page/">{{title}}</a></p>
						<p class="im-bucket-note">{{note}}</p>
						<p class="im-bucket-when">{{when}}</p>
					</li>
					{{/match}}{{/each}}
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="im-bucket-group">
				<p class="im-bucket-head"><span>Cold</span><span>0 of 3 done</span></p>
				<ul class="im-buckets">
					{{#each demo.wishlist}}{{#match group "=" "Cold"}}
					<li class="im-bucket"{{#if state}} data-state="{{state}}"{{/if}}>
						<span class="im-bucket-mark">{{icon "check"}}</span>
						<p class="im-bucket-title"><a href="/collections/wishlist/page/">{{title}}</a></p>
						<p class="im-bucket-note">{{note}}</p>
						<p class="im-bucket-when">{{when}}</p>
					</li>
					{{/match}}{{/each}}
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="im-bucket-group">
				<p class="im-bucket-head"><span>Distance</span><span>0 of 3 done</span></p>
				<ul class="im-buckets">
					{{#each demo.wishlist}}{{#match group "=" "Distance"}}
					<li class="im-bucket"{{#if state}} data-state="{{state}}"{{/if}}>
						<span class="im-bucket-mark">{{icon "check"}}</span>
						<p class="im-bucket-title"><a href="/collections/wishlist/page/">{{title}}</a></p>
						<p class="im-bucket-note">{{note}}</p>
						<p class="im-bucket-when">{{when}}</p>
					</li>
					{{/match}}{{/each}}
				</ul>
			</section>
		</div>
	</article>

	<aside>
		<div class="im-sticky-rail">
			<div class="im-widgets">
				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="b-prog">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="b-prog">How it is going</h2>
					<div class="im-progress" style="--im-value: .11" role="progressbar" aria-valuenow="11" aria-label="Bucket list progress"><span></span></div>
					<p class="text-xs text-muted">1 of 9 done · 2 booked</p>
					<div class="im-widget-stats">
						<div><strong>1</strong><span>Done</span></div>
						<div><strong>2</strong><span>Booked</span></div>
						<div><strong>6</strong><span>Someday</span></div>
					</div>
				</section>

				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="b-done">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="b-done">Already done <a href="/collections/experience/">All</a></h2>
					<ul class="im-widget-list">
						{{#each demo.experience}}{{#match @index "<" 3}}<li><a href="/collections/experience/page/">{{title}}<small>{{where}} · {{when}}</small></a></li>{{/match}}{{/each}}
					</ul>
				</section>

				<section class="im-widget im-widget-fill" aria-labelledby="b-sub">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="b-sub">When one happens</h2>
					<p class="im-widget-heading">I write it up.</p>
					{{> "components/subscribe" id="bucket-email" button="Join"}}
				</section>
			</div>
		</div>
	</aside>
</div>

<section class="im-section im-wrap">
	<div class="im-prose">
		<h2>A checklist, not a shopping list</h2>
		<p>The state is the whole point, so it is the first thing on every row: an empty ring for someday, an accent ring for booked, a filled tick for done. It is the same vocabulary a <a href="/navigation/curriculum/">course lesson</a> uses, because it is the same idea — a thing you have or have not got to yet.</p>
		<div class="im-table-scroll">
		<table>
			<thead><tr><th><code>data-state</code></th><th></th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><em>none</em></td><td>Someday. An empty ring, and the date column says so.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>booked</code></td><td>It is happening: an accent ring, and a real date.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>done</code></td><td>A filled tick, the title struck through but <strong>still legible</strong>, and the date in the success colour.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		</div>

		<h2>Leave the done ones on the page</h2>
		<p>A list that deletes an item the moment it happens is a to-do list. Leaving it — struck through, dated, and linked to the <a href="/collections/experience/">experience</a> it became — is what turns the page into a record of a life rather than a set of intentions.</p>
		<p>That link is the only navigation the collection needs. A done row goes to what happened; the experience page links back to the line it came from.</p>

		<h2>Rules</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Group them by something real.</strong> Water, cold, distance — not "high priority", which is a project-management word and means nothing on a list like this.</li>
			<li><strong>"Someday" is an honest answer.</strong> A made-up date on every line makes the two real dates worth nothing.</li>
			<li><strong>Nine is a list. Forty is a fantasy.</strong></li>
			<li><strong>No prices.</strong> This is not a <a href="/collections/uses/">wish-to-buy</a> page; it is a wish-to-do one.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</section>
